WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.509
I actually have some good news to start with
today.

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:09.050
We have been sort of worried that not enough
people in the United States, in other countries

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.340
as well, but we've been looking at the numbers
in the United States that not enough people

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:18.910
in the U.S. would want the coronavirus vaccine,
which would make it really difficult to get

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:25.180
to the herd immunity that is necessary for
life to really start going back to normal

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.240
in the context of the pandemic.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.950
But the good news is that every single week,
the percentage of Americans that want the

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:38.820
vaccine and plan to get the vaccine and would
accept the vaccine were made available to

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.040
them is going up.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.579
And that's excellent.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.690
That number is now at 71 percent.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.989
71 percent of Americans say they would get
the vaccine.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:52.510
And remember that just months ago, only 40
percent of Americans wanted it.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:59.250
And that crept up to 50 percent, 63, 63 percent
about a month and a half ago.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.010
And that number is now at 71 percent.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:09.730
And the poll that shows 71 percent is from
before Joe Biden and Dr. Anthony Fauci received

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:15.680
their first doses over the last 36 to 48 hours,
which hopefully will push interest in getting

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.860
the vaccine up even further.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:27.960
Now, the 27 percent that remain hesitant about
this vaccine, there's a few characteristics.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.060
These are a few different groups.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:36.300
So those who remain vaccine skeptical are
disproportionately Republicans, disproportionately

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:45.520
those 30 to 49 and disproportionately people
who live rurally and disproportionately black

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.790
American who who are the most vaccine hesitant
groups.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:56.670
Now, the reasons why each of these groups
is hesitant about the vaccine differ.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:03.330
Some of the primary reasons are fear of side
effects, fear that the vaccine is too new,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.400
which can mean a lot of different things.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.930
But that's the way they described it.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:14.569
And among black Americans, the primary reasons
for vaccine coronavirus vaccine hesitancy

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:22.980
are general distrust of vaccines and concerns
that one could get coronavirus from the coronavirus

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.980
vaccine.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:29.440
Now, in terms of states, I don't this is not
super surprising, but there's some interesting

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.730
data points here based on data from the IHT
from a few days ago.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:42.190
The states where residents most want the vaccine
are Vermont, New York, Minnesota, Washington

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:49.580
State, California, Hawaii, Virginia and Colorado,
followed closely by sort of the rest of the

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.420
northeast states, plus North Carolina and
a few others.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:59.019
Now, on the other side of this, the states
who residents least want the vaccine at the

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:03.370
absolute bottom of the list are Mississippi,
Arkansas and Wisconsin.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:08.319
Now, I'm guessing that there are particulars
about why Wisconsin is there.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:13.209
I don't know if maybe Wisconsin has a number
of different religious groups and sects there.

00:03:13.209 --> 00:03:16.720
I don't know if there's one that is overwhelmingly
anti vaccine.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:18.680
I'd be interested in knowing more about that.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:23.390
But Mississippi, Arkansas and Wisconsin are
the most the states most least interested

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:29.190
in the coronavirus vaccine, followed by a
number of states like Texas, South Carolina,

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.730
Georgia, Alabama, Ohio, Indiana, Oklahoma,
Kansas.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:37.400
So there's quite a long list in sort of that
lower but not lowest range.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.870
So bottom line, it's good that the numbers
are up to 71 percent.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:46.400
I do want to remind you the vaccine is not
going to be given to kids anytime soon.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.180
So when we talk about 70 percent of herd immunity,
we're talking about the whole country.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:58.440
So 71 percent of adults wanting and getting
the vaccine eventually doesn't get us to 70

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.660
percent of the entire country.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.340
We still would not be at herd immunity.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.170
But these are the best numbers we've had since
the start of this thing.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.459
And that's good.

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:11.660
The public campaigns to say I got the vaccine
and people posting pictures on on Facebook

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.539
and social media, Dr. Fauci, getting the vaccine,
et cetera, that does seem to be working because

00:04:17.539 --> 00:04:25.270
getting a vaccine in the abstract before anybody's
getting it is not likely to appeal to as many

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.560
people as getting the vaccine that my twelve
nurse friends got and posted on Facebook about.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.569
And that's certainly helping.

00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:40.840
Now, as of this morning, 777 thousand Americans
have received the first dose of the vaccine.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:45.389
That's zero point two, three percent of the
U.S. population.

00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:47.189
It's a start.

00:04:47.189 --> 00:04:52.680
But again, unless and we're expecting to unless
we ramp up the number of vaccines going out

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:57.869
and being used to inoculate people, every
week goes up.

00:04:57.869 --> 00:04:58.869
It's going to take a while.

00:04:58.869 --> 00:04:59.869
It's.

00:04:59.869 --> 00:05:02.689
Going to be a process now in terms of more
vaccines, remember that currently in the US

00:05:02.689 --> 00:05:08.009
there's the Pfizer Bion tech vaccine and the
Moderna vaccines that have been approved.

00:05:08.009 --> 00:05:12.190
The Moderna vaccine is just now starting to
be given to people.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:16.559
And then we have the AstraZeneca Oxford vaccine
close to possible approval.

00:05:16.559 --> 00:05:21.370
And then behind that, you've got the Novavax
and Johnson and Johnson vaccines moving ahead,

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.409
pending results.

00:05:22.409 --> 00:05:28.449
So in the end, whatever the polls say, start
distributing it, get it to people, keep the

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:32.569
process moving forward, and we'll keep evaluating
month to month and really week to week.

00:05:32.569 --> 00:05:35.849
Now, an important note, and I don't understand
this yet.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:36.849
I've seen the data.

00:05:36.849 --> 00:05:42.149
I don't I haven't interpreted the data, even
though states have now.

00:05:42.149 --> 00:05:48.680
It's been several days, in fact, more than
that since states received their first shipments.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:54.979
Many states have only so far actually used
10 to 15 percent of the vaccines that they've

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:55.979
received.

00:05:55.979 --> 00:06:03.110
Now, I express concern that we don't want
to see lots of vaccines just sitting around

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.360
and not being used.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.349
And a lot of this is getting the logistics
up and running.

00:06:06.349 --> 00:06:07.749
And I understand that.

00:06:07.749 --> 00:06:14.279
But over time, if if we are seeing that states
are sitting on a bunch of vaccine with lack

00:06:14.279 --> 00:06:22.219
of clarity or poor execution in terms of actually
getting it to people, that will be a concern.

00:06:22.219 --> 00:06:24.389
And we'll cross that that bridge when we come
to it.

00:06:24.389 --> 00:06:26.410
But the urgency can't be exaggerated.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:31.360
Another 3400 people died yesterday of the
virus.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:07:35.830
Absolutely tragic numbers.

